'''''Goeppertia lietzei''''' (syn. ''Calathea lietzei'') is a species of plant belonging to the genus ''[[Goeppertia]]'' of the [[Marantaceae]] [[Family (taxonomy)|family]], [[native plant|native]] to eastern Brazil.<ref>{{Cite web |title=Goeppertia lietzei (É.Morren) Saka {{!}} Plants of the World Online {{!}} Kew Science |url=http://powo.science.kew.org/taxon/urn:lsid:ipni.org:names:77174968-1 |access-date=2026-06-04 |website=Plants of the World Online |language=en}}</ref>

''Goeppertia lietzei'' has been introduced to El Salvador, Honduras, and Mexico.<ref name="77174968-1" /><ref name="EPPO">{{cite web |title=Goeppertia lietzei(CBALI) |url=https://gd.eppo.int/taxon/CBALI |website=EPPO Global Database |access-date=19 November 2025}}</ref> It can be considered [[invasive species|invasive]] in West Java, Indonesia.<ref name="Handayani">{{cite journal |last1=Handayani |first1=A |last2=Junaedi |first2=D I |last3=Zuhud |first3=E A M |title=Ecological risk assessment of potentially invasive alien plant species in Cibodas Biosphere Reserve, West Java, Indonesia |journal=IOP Conf. Series: Earth and Environmental Science |date=2021 |volume=914 |issue=012035 |doi=10.1088/1755-1315/914/1/012035|doi-access=free }}</ref><ref name="Kudo">{{cite journal |last1=Kudo |first1=Yoshihumi |last2=Mutaqien |first2=Zaenal |last3=Simbolon |first3=Herwint |last4=Suzuki |first4=Eizi |title=Spread of invasive plants along trails in two national parks in West Java, Indonesia |journal=TROPICS |date=2014 |volume=23 |issue=3 |pages=99-110 |url=https://www.jstage.jst.go.jp/article/tropics/23/3/23_99/_pdf}}</ref> It has also been reported as growing in disturbed forest in East Kalimantan, Indonesia.<ref name="Fiqa">{{cite journal |last1=Fiqa |first1=Abban Putri |last2=Fauziah |last3=Lestari |first3=Dewi Ayu |last4=Budiharta |first4=Sugeng |title=The importance of in-situ conservation area in mining concession in preserving diversity, threatened and potential floras in East Kalimantan, Indonesia |journal=Biodiversitas |date=2019 |volume=20 |issue=1 |pages=198-210}}</ref> In Indonesia, it is locally known as ''Kalatea batik''.<ref name="Prihatini">{{cite journal |last1=Prihatini |first1=Juliati |last2=Iskandar |first2=Johan |last3=Partasasmita |first3=Ruhyat |last4=Nurjaman |first4=Deden |title=The impacts of traditional homegarden conversion into the commercial one: A case study in Sukapura Village of the Upstream Citarum Watershed, West Java, Indonesia |journal=Biodiversitas |date=2018 |volume=19 |issue=5 |pages=1926-1940 |doi=10.13057/biodiv/d190545|doi-access=free }}</ref><ref name="Febrianti">{{cite journal |last1=Febrianti |first1=Deliana |last2=Harisandy |first2=Muhammad Dandi |last3=Suwardi |first3=Adi Bejo |title=The diversity of plant species in the ecotourism zone of Gunung Leuser National Park, Tangkahan, Indonesia |journal=Jurnal Biologi Tropis |date=2022 |volume=22 |issue=2 |pages=434 – 440 |url=https://www.researchgate.net/profile/Adi-Bejo-Suwardi/publication/359700544_The_diversity_of_plant_species_in_the_ecotourism_zone_of_Gunung_Leuser_National_Park_Tangkahan_Indonesia/links/624977a45e2f8c7a03569765/The-diversity-of-plant-species-in-the-ecotourism-zone-of-Gunung-Leuser-National-Park-Tangkahan-Indonesia.pdf}}</ref>

== Description ==
[[File:Maranta lietzei kz01.jpg|left|thumb|251x251px|Inflorescence of '''''Goeppertia lietzei''''']]
'''''Goeppertia lietzei''''' is a medium sized species with pointy, long, dark green [[Leaf|leaves]], with a long, think, green or purple [[Petiole (botany)|petioles]] and a green or purple, short [[pulvinus]]. It has a pattern on the surface of the leaves with straight, light green bands appearing from the middle vein to the sides of the leaf. The [[inflorescence]] of ''Goeppertia lietzei'' is made of multiple [[Bract|bracts]] on a long, thin [[Peduncle (botany)|peduncle]]. The bracts are green, sometimes a bit hairy and the [[Flower|flowers]] are fully white.<ref>{{Cite journal |last=Morren |first=Charles |last2=Morren |first2=Edouard |date=1875 |title=Nouvelles Marantacées du Bresil, à feuillage orné et coloré, |url=https://www.biodiversitylibrary.org/page/43062527 |journal=Belgique horticole |volume=25 |pages=273}}</ref>

== Cultivation ==
While many of cultivars like "White Fusion" and else are sold as ''Goeppertia lietzei'' on the market, those are actually all cultivars of ''[[Goeppertia albertii]]''. This confusion came from the original google patent of the White Fusion cultivar which stated that it came from a selection of ''Calathea lietzei'', but they were stating this without any inflroescence confirmation. Later flowering specimens made it clear that the google patent was wrong. ''Goeppertia lietzei'' does have a variegated cultivar, but it is not wildely sold on the market and is very rare to find in cultivation.{{fact|date=June 2026}}

